# FINNEST — web-app (TanStack Start) environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# On Vercel, add the same keys under
#   Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables
#
# IMPORTANT
# - The VITE_ prefixed keys are PUBLIC. They are baked into the browser bundle
#   at build time and are safe to expose. They must be the *publishable* key
#   (sb_publishable_...), never a service_role / secret key.
# - The un-prefixed keys are SERVER-ONLY. They are read by Nitro at runtime.
#   Never prefix them with VITE_, and never paste them into client code.
# - VITE_* values are frozen into the bundle at BUILD time. After changing one
#   you must redeploy (or rebuild), a plain restart is not enough.

# ---------- Public / browser ----------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://wyjjzynjoorjmpffndzu.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_Nzb2UydbWvi6wJTtdt0_oA_pRuAWfWf

# ---------- Server only (Nitro runtime) ----------
SUPABASE_URL=https://wyjjzynjoorjmpffndzu.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_Nzb2UydbWvi6wJTtdt0_oA_pRuAWfWf

# Only needed if you switch the server functions to the admin client
# (src/integrations/supabase/client.server.ts). It bypasses RLS.
# Never set this on the web/ project and never expose it to the browser.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=sb_secret_...
